2026-11-13T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2491) 'How the machine sits in the model
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2491) 'qwenputer (MIT) compiles a circuit into the two sublayers of a Gated DeltaNet layer. An MLP unit
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2491) 'is a lookup, and a recurrent head is a table whose rows a one-hot key overwrites. No weight is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2491) 'trained. The processor's registers, ROM and RAM are the heads' state rows.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2491) 'A run looks like this in the token stream. The body writes a tool call in its own syntax. The
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2491) 'tower copies each token of the call into a text buffer. At the closing tag the tower takes over
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2491) 'and emits chip tokens, one record per instruction. Each byte the firmware prints comes back as
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2491) 'the body's own token for that byte, so the body reads a tool response it wrote itself. Chip
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2491) 'tokens run through the tower only. The body's layers, cache and positions see the text alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2491) 'Why the tower is a separate component
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2491) 'Upstream widens the host model and puts the processor in the added residual dims. Bonsai 2
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2491) 'cannot take that route:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2491) '- The body is Hadamard-rotated ternary in 1024-column blocks. Zero padding, mute columns and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2491) '  rescaled norm gains do not survive that packing word for word.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2491) '- The engine's kernels are registered for the body's hidden size.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2491) '- The chip token rows hold values such as 2^40, which are not ternary.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2491) 'So the tower keeps its own residual stream of 1280 dims, its own token table and its own
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2491) 'states, and the body stays byte-identical. This is upstream's own fast decoding path, which
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2491) 'already runs the chip layers as a second view with a second cache.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2491) 'The circuit is compiled for Bonsai 2's head geometry (16 key heads, 48 value heads, head
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2491) 'dim 128, conv kernel 4), so the engine's recurrent kernels run it. The MLP is cut from the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2491) 'body's 17408 units to the 8576 the circuit uses.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

