2026-11-13T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2491) 'Ternary planes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2491) 'Every tower matrix is a sum of ternary planes: weights in {-1, 0, +1} with one scale per
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2491) 'row and group of 128 columns, or per column and group of 128 rows where that needs fewer
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2491) 'planes. Each weight sits in one plane, so the sum equals the matrix bit for bit. Of the 89
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2491) 'matrices, 82 need at most two planes and none needs more than seven.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2491) 'The scales are not binary16 values: they range from 2^-41 to 2^125. A ternary tower therefore
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2491) 'needs a plane format with bf16 scales and no Hadamard rotation, which the artifact container
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2491) 'does not have yet. Until it does, the tower is stored dense.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

