 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:59Z (RFD66606-2491) '- **Served.** `ninfer-serve --chip calc-bridge` at temperature 0, twelve arithmetic prompts:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:00Z (RFD66606-2491) '  21 bursts and 80,468 chip tokens, each served token equal to the reference machine's when it
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:01Z (RFD66606-2491) '  is fed the model's own call tokens. All twelve values equal Python's, and a power too large
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:02Z (RFD66606-2491) '  for the firmware returns its `error`. Controls: without `--chip` the call comes back
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

