2026-11-13T00:02:09Z (RFD66606-2491) 'Serving
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:10Z (RFD66606-2491) '`--chip NAME` selects a firmware and adds the calc tool to a request that declares none. The
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:11Z (RFD66606-2491) 'answered call is returned inline in the content: the call, the tool response the firmware
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:12Z (RFD66606-2491) 'printed, then the model's answer. `--chip-trace FILE` writes each burst's tokens.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:13Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:14Z (RFD66606-2491) 'A `--chip` server has one request lane and one device. It runs with no drafter or with the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:15Z (RFD66606-2491) 'DFlash2 drafter at up to 11 draft tokens. Any other combination stops at startup. A request
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:16Z (RFD66606-2491) 'whose echo is cut by the output limit ends with the limit reason.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:17Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:18Z (RFD66606-2491) 'On one RTX 4090 a burst runs at 500 chip tokens per second. Text decodes at 93 to 99 tokens
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:19Z (RFD66606-2491) 'per second with `--chip` and DFlash2 at five draft tokens, at 69 to 71 with `--chip` and no
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:20Z (RFD66606-2491) 'drafter, and at 171 to 190 on the server of RFD66606-2311 without the tower.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:21Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:22Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:23Z (RFD66606-2491) 'Drafting beside the tower
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:24Z (RFD66606-2491) 'A DFlash2 round commits at most one token more than its draft tokens. While a tool call is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:25Z (RFD66606-2491) 'open, the server gives a round a budget of one token, so the round carries no draft and the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:26Z (RFD66606-2491) 'closing tag is the last token of its round. The burst starts there. The echo is forced
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:27Z (RFD66606-2491) 'through the text model by the path the thinking-budget close uses, and that path also
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:28Z (RFD66606-2491) 'appends the drafter's context.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:29Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:30Z (RFD66606-2491) 'The budget of one starts in the round after the opening tag. A round that held the opening
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:31Z (RFD66606-2491) 'tag, the closing tag and one more token would commit text before the echo. The shortest
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:32Z (RFD66606-2491) 'well-formed call is 12 tokens, and a round at 11 draft tokens holds 12, so no well-formed
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:33Z (RFD66606-2491) 'call fits. A malformed call shorter than a round is detected and counted, not prevented.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:34Z (RFD66606-2491) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:35Z (RFD66606-2491) 'Served with DFlash2 at five draft tokens, 47 bursts and 121,346 chip tokens equal the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:36Z (RFD66606-2491) 'reference machine's, 34 of 34 prompts equal Python, no round commits more than one token
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:37Z (RFD66606-2491) 'while a call is open, and no owned position is skipped. Controls: with the budget of one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:38Z (RFD66606-2491) 'switched off by a test option, 234 rounds commit more than one token while a call is open,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:39Z (RFD66606-2491) 'and with the ROM word spoiled every burst differs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2491  1 LINE
 Text:Written

